    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add vertically-oriented table cells sub-feature to writing-mode]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30702</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30702"/>
        <updated>2026-09-29T22:43:21.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83347420?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #29241.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4064318473" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241">#29241</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Following the guidance in the issue, this adds a <code class="notranslate">vertical_oriented_table_cells</code> sub-feature to <code class="notranslate">css.properties.writing-mode</code>, mirroring the existing <code class="notranslate">vertical_oriented_form_controls</code> sub-feature.</p>
<p dir="auto">Data and sources:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Chrome 92</strong>: verified by testing in the issue; tracking bug referenced via <code class="notranslate">impl_url</code> (<a href="https://crbug.com/40183612" rel="nofollow">crbug.com/40183612</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Firefox 47</strong>: supports vertical table cells, but rendering is not always correct (see screenshot in the issue), so it is marked as <code class="notranslate">partial_implementation</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Safari 17.4</strong>: marked as <code class="notranslate">partial_implementation</code>. The change enabling vertical writing modes for table cells (<a href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/0d695812f5b0daef531a9760903457364d2265ff">WebKit commit 0d69581</a>) shipped in the WebKit 618.1.10 branch (Safari 17.4), but the follow-up fix was reverted in <a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=266941" rel="nofollow">bug 266941</a> and the tracking bug <a href="https://webkit.org/b/266928" rel="nofollow">266928</a> is still open, so support remains incomplete. The note on the entry explains that vertical writing modes were not applied to <code class="notranslate">th</code> and <code class="notranslate">td</code> elements before Safari 17.4, as requested in the issue.</li>
<li>All other browsers use <code class="notranslate">mirror</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Questions for reviewers:</p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Should Firefox's <code class="notranslate">partial_implementation</code> flag start at 47, or is there a later version where rendering is correct?</li>
<li>The issue title says "iOS &lt; 17", but based on the WebKit commit history, 17.4 seems to be the first version with any (partial) support — Safari iOS therefore mirrors 17.4.</li>
</ol>
<h3 dir="auto">Release note</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>CSS: Added <code class="notranslate">vertical_oriented_table_cells</code> subfeature to <code class="notranslate">writing-mode</code>.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
