        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 150 focusgroup global attribute]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30671</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30671"/>
        <updated>2026-09-25T10:43:32.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 150 adds support for the <code class="notranslate">focusgroup</code> global attribute, the related <code class="notranslate">focusgroupstart</code> global attribute, and their reflected DOM properties. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5637601087193088" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5637601087193088</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds support for the four features listed above. In particular, for the <code class="notranslate">focusgroup</code> attribute, I've added an individual datapoint for each of the attribute's <a href="https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/#focusgroup-tokens" rel="nofollow">tokens</a> and <a href="https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/#supported-behaviors" rel="nofollow">behaviors</a>. I have given the behaviors a prefix so they will all be kept together in the BCD table.</p>
<p dir="auto">Notes:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The features are currently listed as non-standard because the spec PR is still open: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3466650602" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11723" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/html/pull/11723/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11723">whatwg/html#11723</a>.</li>
<li>I am currently working on documenting only the <a href="https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/" rel="nofollow">v1 focusgroup</a> features, which are all implemented. The <a href="https://open-ui.org/components/focusgroup-v2.explainer/" rel="nofollow">v2 focusgroup</a> features are currently experimental and subject to change, so I will handle them in a separate project in the future.</li>
<li>The WebIDL for the DOM properties is listed in the <a href="https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/#feature-detection" rel="nofollow">feature detection</a> section of the explainer.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">cc <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/janewman/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/janewman">@janewman</a> for technical input/questions. If you could check these to make sure I've not missed anything, that would be much appreciated. Thanks!</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
